regiondemagallanes-by-faemiyah for Debian
----------------------------------------

This is a standard version of the 4K intro, not the minimized "party" version.

The source code uses the USE_LD definition and does not generate music.
Instead, it relies on the precalculated soundtrack and on the shader files
installed in /usr/share/regiondemagallanes-by-faemiyah.

The upstream soundtrack is a 32-bit float WAV file (about 31 MB). It is
compressed to FLAC at build time (about 18 MB), and the intro decodes it at
startup with libsndfile (debian/patches/06_load-flac-soundtrack.patch).
The soundtrack peaks at exactly 0 dBFS: a few hundred samples are clipped
by one 24-bit step in the FLAC file, which is inaudible.

I always prefer using the most basic binary format to ensure compatibility
with dh_shlibdeps, allowing it to accurately identify dependencies.

Forcing music generation might be possible, but exploring the ASM code
suggests a loss of cross-platform compilation.

Keys: F toggles fullscreen (the picture keeps its aspect ratio, with black
bars), Esc quits. VSync is requested at startup
(debian/patches/07_enable-vsync.patch).

The upstream archive also ships the Windows and FreeBSD builds of the
intro, and the Windows SDL2.dll. They are kept in the orig tarball as
shipped upstream and are not installed.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

